description: Decisions requiring explicit human approval before implementation
alwaysApply: true
---

# Full stop — ask before proceeding

Post the question and wait. Do not implement, do not propose-and-proceed.

1. Changing any metric definition in PROPOSAL §6
2. Changing the abstain threshold or abstain behavior (§7.4)
3. Adding, removing, or rewording any query in `config/queries.yaml`
4. Generating, labeling, or modifying ANY eval case (§8)
5. Swapping or adding a SERP provider
6. Any write, edit, or delete under `data/raw/`
7. Adding a dependency not already in `pyproject.toml`
8. Anything touching auth, tenancy, user accounts, or a hosted dashboard
9. Wording of the README headline finding or any report copy
10. Changing what a verdict class means (§7.4)

# Green light — proceed without asking

Refactors within a module, test additions, type hints, docstrings, logging,
error handling, formatting, dependency version pins, CLI ergonomics,
performance work that doesn't change output values.

# Never silently

If a spec section is ambiguous, contradictory, or silent on what you need —
stop and say which section and what's missing. Do not pick the reasonable
interpretation and continue.
